This flow diagram outlines the necessary interventions for problem identification and fixing when monitoring the processor temperature. The process starts by monitoring the temperature, reading the system error log, and reading the system load. If there is an error, system processes are ended. If the load is high, the maximum processor usage is lowered. If the temperature is high and the load is not high, the fan speed is increased. If the temperature remains high despite increasing the fan speed, the room temperature is lowered.

